@startuml
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

title Frontier Research Landscape: VLA and Related Paradigms

package "Foundational Learning Paradigms" {
    [Deep Reinforcement Learning\n(DRL)]
    [World Models]
    [Large Language Models\n(LLM)]
    [Multimodal Models\n(VLM / MLLM)]
}

package "Embodied Intelligence" {
    [Embodied AI]
}

package "Action-Centric Models" {
    [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)]
}

' ---- Core relationships ----

[Deep Reinforcement Learning\n(DRL)] --> [World Models] : model-based RL
[World Models] --> [Deep Reinforcement Learning\n(DRL)] : planning / imagination

[Large Language Models\n(LLM)] --> [Multimodal Models\n(VLM / MLLM)] : vision grounding
[Multimodal Models\n(VLM / MLLM)] --> [Large Language Models\n(LLM)] : semantic supervision

[Multimodal Models\n(VLM / MLLM)] --> [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)] : perceptual & semantic backbone
[Large Language Models\n(LLM)] --> [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)] : task & instruction grounding

[Deep Reinforcement Learning\n(DRL)] --> [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)] : policy optimization / fine-tuning
[World Models] --> [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)] : latent dynamics / rollout augmentation

[Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)] --> [Embodied AI] : language-grounded control
[Embodied AI] --> [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)] : embodiment constraints

' ---- Conceptual notes ----

note right of [Vision-Language-Action Models\n(VLA)]
VLA learns:
p(action | vision, language, history)

Language directly shapes
the action distribution.
end note

note left of [World Models]
World Models learn:
p(next_state | state, action)

Focus: physical dynamics
end note

note left of [Large Language Models\n(LLM)]
LLMs learn:
p(token | context)

Focus: symbolic reasoning
and compositionality
end note

note bottom of [Deep Reinforcement Learning\n(DRL)]
DRL optimizes:
Expected return

Focus: control & exploration
end note

note right of [Multimodal Models\n(VLM / MLLM)]
Multimodal Models learn:
cross-modal alignment

Focus: perception & semantics
end note

@enduml
